At 08:05 14/06/2002, Peter Watkinson sent this up the stick:

>Hi Folks,
>
>Upgraded to Woody from potato using a mixture of Apt-Get, upgrade and -f 
>install and dselect everything seems to be working fine except a few 
>problems with unpacking. Now how do I upgrade the kernel? Is there a nice 
>easy way?

apt-get install make-kpkg

Then you cd into /usr/src/ , bunzip2 and untar the source, make config (or 
menuconfig or xconfig).  Here comes the magic :)

make-kpkg --revision=<your version> kernel-image

Bear in mind that I don't use modules, and you'll need to read the manpage 
should you ant to incorporate any Debian-provided patches.  then it is a 
simple matter of using dpkg to install the deb thats remained in /usr/src

Cheers,
Rob


